1aefff5d7295"],

Cell["1. Mathematical Background", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"57bc29bb-681e-704a-a201-266c5ce96001"],

Cell["\<\
The toolkit works sector by sector. A sector is labeled by {nh, Nd}, where nh \
is the number of graviton fields h and Nd is the total number of derivatives. \
The starting point is the finite-dimensional vector space of local scalar \
operators in that sector.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c6f4020-468e-7b4a-b9f0-23f96b3d5eb5"],

Cell["\<\
Eq. (1)   V_(nh,Nd) := span of local scalar monomials built from nh gravitons \
and Nd derivatives.\
\>", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"83087e25-12b0-6845-9ae3-f5aa3a2bb50d"],

Cell["\<\
The raw basis generated by the code is a concrete spanning set for V_(nh,Nd). \
It is obtained by distributing Nd derivatives among nh fields in all ordered \
ways, forming the corresponding derivative-decorated monomials, and then \
taking all scalar contractions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"532549f0-aa7c-0849-af36-b0637e83617d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  {EdgeForm[{GrayLevel[0.45], Thickness[0.003]}], FaceForm[RGBColor[
   0.8300000000000001, 0.8900000000000001, 0.944]], 
   RectangleBox[{0, 0}, {10, 6}], 
   {FaceForm[RGBColor[0.97, 0.905, 0.7949999999999999]], 
    RectangleBox[{1., 0.9}, {4.5, 2.2}]}, 
   {FaceForm[RGBColor[0.8, 0.905, 0.8425]], 
    RectangleBox[{5.9, 2.8}, {8.8, 4.1}], InsetBox[
     StyleBox["\<\"V_(nh,Nd)\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontSize->16,
      FontWeight->Bold], {8.3, 5.3}], InsetBox[
     StyleBox["\<\"T_(nh,Nd)\\n(total derivatives)\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontSize->12], {2.75, 1.55}], InsetBox[
     StyleBox["\<\"R_(nh,Nd)\\n(redefinition image)\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontSize->12], {7.35, 3.45}], InsetBox[
     StyleBox["\<\"First quotient:\\nV / T\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontSize->13,
      FontWeight->Bold], {6., 1.2}], ArrowBox[{{4.75, 1.55}, {5.45, 1.55}}], 
    InsetBox[
     StyleBox["\<\"Then quotient by R\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontSize->12], {7.25, 1.55}]}},
  ImageSize->560,
  PlotRange->{{-0.2, 10.2}, {-0.2, 6.2}}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->\
"c68357eb-4b34-9b47-a86f-b167bd2da628"],

Cell["\<\
The first physical equivalence is integration by parts. Two Lagrangians \
define the same action if they differ by a total derivative.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c2e7727-383b-d14a-94dc-775943c490a1"],

Cell["Eq. (2)   L ~ L + d_mu K^mu.", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"12b3b8d6-8e95-7745-becc-25cbb19f038a"],

Cell["\<\
Let T_(nh,Nd) denote the subspace of total derivatives inside V_(nh,Nd). The \
physically relevant space after IBP is the quotient V_(nh,Nd) / T_(nh,Nd).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d88caee8-183e-5746-a23a-eea95664191a"],

Cell["Eq. (3)   Q_(nh,Nd) := V_(nh,Nd) / T_(nh,Nd).", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a2a07769-cd3f-5240-a5ff-e2a1ae76e020"],

Cell["\<\
The code identifies T_(nh,Nd) through the Euler-Lagrange operator. A local \
scalar density is a total derivative exactly when its Euler derivative \
vanishes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b1df3fce-0191-474c-88de-e30dd1d62ec7"],

Cell["\<\
Eq. (4)   L in T_(nh,Nd)  iff  delta L / delta h_(mu nu) = 0.\
\>", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bd9fc1b7-1b3c-f64e-8456-02a2d35cff67"],

Cell["\<\
This is why IBPData constructs a generic linear combination of raw basis \
elements and solves VarD[h][L] == 0. The null space of that linear map is the \
space of IBP relations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6eacc14c-302d-5944-805a-d81b69dd5f19"],

Cell["\<\
The second equivalence is field redefinition redundancy. For a local \
symmetric rank-2 tensor Delta h_(mu nu), the quadratic Fierz-Pauli Lagrangian \
changes by an equation-of-motion term plus a total derivative.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"72f57b64-70fc-8c4c-b3c5-f40f580a7cf0"],

Cell["\<\
Eq. (5)   delta L_FP = E_FP^(mu nu) Delta h_(mu nu) + d_mu K^mu.\
\>", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8aed3a67-7e0c-ab47-891a-e48114ad8cd4"],

Cell["\<\
Therefore the image of the linear map Delta h -> E_FP^(mu nu) Delta h_(mu nu) \
is redundant inside the IBP quotient.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d2c4e1e9-4fa5-af46-8dd9-a8282f264799"],

Cell["\<\
Eq. (6)   R_(nh,Nd) := Im(F_(nh-1,Nd-2 -> nh,Nd)) subset Q_(nh,Nd).\
\>", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"38d6ef6c-ceaf-b348-afcc-1c6fec5f59fb"],

Cell["\<\
For interaction sectors, the final basis is the quotient of the IBP quotient \
by this image.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"862107a7-6dc2-a043-ab83-a861310fc6e4"],

Cell["Eq. (7)   P_(nh,Nd) := Q_(nh,Nd) / R_(nh,Nd).", "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e8eca381-7bb5-7f43-9ba6-9eccdebe85ba"],

Cell["\<\
Quadratic sectors are intentionally treated differently. A linear field \
redefinition acts directly on the kinetic operator itself, so quotienting the \
quadratic sector by those directions is usually not the desired equivalence \
relation for the kinetic term.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d257c62d-d02a-7b40-bd56-6a5928f7ba7b"],

Cell["Eq. (8)   nh < 3: use Q_(nh,Nd);   nh >= 3: use P_(nh,Nd).", \
"DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"3b0d9635-2834-5e42-9357-35b1b15700bb"],

Cell["\<\
The diagrams above summarize the two quotient operations: a kernel quotient \
for IBP and an image quotient for interaction-level field redefinitions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6156d263-cee1-9d42-a7ad-f7a07f176185"],

Cell["", "PageBreak",ExpressionUUID->"1b0e732d-6019-a24b-9cae-f651f661b3e4"],

Cell["2. User Guide and Code Reference", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4505e39b-a886-a644-83f1-bc234d72620c"],

Cell["\<\
The normal workflow is: load the toolkit, compute sector data once with \
caching, inspect the basis of a sector if needed, and then reduce a \
Lagrangian either sector by sector or automatically.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36c8d7b4-7eaf-3548-8a2e-520fb8c293fa"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Get[\"graviton_basis_toolkit.wl\"]",
 FontFamily->"Courier New",
 FontSize->10]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4633129-a5d1-5745-9536-\
56eaae9c3db0"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["res = RunBasisComputation[\n  \"MaxDimension\" -> 5,\n\
  \"CacheDirectory\" -> FileNameJoin[{Directory[], \"basis_cache\"}],\n  \
\"UseCache\" -> True,\n  \"Verbose\" -> True\n];",
 FontFamily->"Courier New",
 FontSize->10]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"87f43e76-dc3d-0e4c-a381-\
694e3ff77897"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["red = ReduceLagrangian[lag,\n  \"CacheDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{Directory[], \"basis_cache\"}],\n  \"UseCache\" -> True\n];\n\n\
red[\"ReducedExpression\"]",
 FontFamily->"Courier New",
 FontSize->10]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f34f0f7-4c0e-7f4b-aa06-\
44a3cdbae86c"],

Cell["\<\
The public functions most users actually need are summarized below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6cfddcc6-0bba-6a41-8426-024090a85cc6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Function\"\>", "\<\"Role\"\>"},
    {"\<\"RunBasisComputation\"\>", "\<\"Compute and cache sector data over a \
sector list.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"ComputeSectorData\"\>", "\<\"Assemble the raw basis, IBP quotient, \
redefinition image, and physical basis of one sector.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"RawBasisOfSector\"\>", "\<\"Return the raw scalar basis of a stored \
sector.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"IBPBasisOfSector\"\>", "\<\"Return the IBP quotient basis of a \
stored sector.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"PhysicalBasisOfSector\"\>", "\<\"Return the final basis after the \
interaction-sector field-redefinition quotient.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"RedefinitionRulesOfSector\"\>", "\<\"Return explicit independent \
field redefinitions and their images in the IBP basis.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"ReduceSectorLagrangian\"\>", "\<\"Reduce a known single-sector \
expression modulo IBP and field redefinitions.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"ReduceLagrangian\"\>", "\<\"Split a general expression by sector \
and reduce each sector automatically.\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {None, {
        RGBColor[0.975, 0.975, 0.975]}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxItemStyle->{"Columns" -> {{
        Directive[FontFamily -> "Source Sans Pro", 11]}}, "Rows" -> {{
        Directive[FontFamily -> "Source Sans Pro", 11]}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"800cca36-7425-6044-ab99-d448ae57506c"],

